---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AuthorHeader from '../components/AuthorHeader.astro';
import SubscribeForm from '../components/SubscribeForm.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Mara Voss, an independent designer and developer in Copenhagen."
>
  <AuthorHeader compact showBio={false} showSubscribe={false} />

  <section class="about">
    <p class="about__eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="about__title">{site.name}</h1>
    <p class="about__lede">
      I make small, deliberate software for the web — and write about the parts
      that don’t fit in a changelog.
    </p>

    <div class="about__body">
      <p>
        I’m an independent designer and developer in Copenhagen. For the past
        decade I’ve worked at the seam between design and engineering: drawing
        the interface, writing the front end, and staying close enough to the
        backend to know when a simpler idea would be better.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before working for myself, I led design at a small product studio and
        spent a few years as a freelance developer. I’ve shipped tools for
        writers, researchers, and people who make things with their hands. The
        common thread is a preference for software that is quiet, legible, and
        built to last longer than the average launch cycle.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is my notebook. It is a place for essays, observations, and
        the occasional field report. No growth hacks, no algorithmic feed, no
        reason for it to exist other than the pleasure of putting a thought
        somewhere it can be found again.
      </p>

      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p>
        I’m building <em>Lumen</em>, a writing app for people who want fewer
        features and more room to think. I take on a small number of design and
        development projects each quarter. I’m also slowly restoring a 1987
        bicycle, which is teaching me more about maintenance than any software
        book has.
      </p>

      <h2>A few beliefs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The best interface is the one you stop noticing.</li>
        <li>Small teams with long horizons make the most coherent things.</li>
        <li>Software should let you leave without making you feel guilty.</li>
        <li>The web is better when more of it belongs to individuals.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        You can write to me at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. I read everything and
        reply when I can. For new posts, use the <a href="/feed.xml">RSS feed</a> or
        subscribe below.
      </p>

      <h2>Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and
        plain CSS. Posts live in typed data rather than Markdown files. There is
        no database, no tracking, and no JavaScript except the small script that
        makes the subscribe form say hello.
      </p>
    </div>

    <SubscribeForm />
  </section>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
